OL,3,AUS death row inmate Christa Pike awake
OL,4,Aand speaking after failed execution,
OL,5,Alawyers say
OL,6,
OL,7,FUS death row inmate Christa Pike is
OL,8,F"conscious and speaking" after
OL,9,Fsurviving a failed execution attempt in
OL,10,FTennessee last week, her lawyers say.
OL,12,FPike, 50, continues to receive critical
OL,13,Fmedical care while "handcuffed and
OL,14,Fshackled to the bed" in hospital, her
OL,15,Flawyers said in a statement on Tuesday.
OL,16,FAn anaesthesiologist advising her team
OL,17,Ftold the BBC that Pike was able to
OL,18,Fcommunicate in a "basic way" but did
OL,19,Fnot seem to recall the execution
OL,20,Fattempt.
OL,23,APub: 06-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG9/40
